<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">Having made a passing reference to Mick Fl=
eetwood in Tuesday=E2=80=99s thrilling edition of your favourite email, Foo=
tball Daily genuinely wasn=E2=80=99t expecting to be repeatedly typing that=
 particular F-word in our lead story in today=E2=80=99s edition. While we w=
ere aware Arsenal were in the coastal town of Fleetwood for a Fizzy Cup tie=
 that could scarcely have been less glamorous than the previous evening=E2=
=80=99s Ballon d=E2=80=99Or ceremony at the Palladium, the needle on our pa=
tented Potential Shock-o-Meter had barely moved before a match pitting the =
Premier League champions against a side struggling in League Two. Even with=
 the residual winds from Storm Boelo still buffeting the ground, we presume=
d Arsenal=E2=80=99s second string would have enough about them to record a =
comfortable win at Highbury, over 20 years after they left a London stadium=
 of the same name to begin their residency at the Emirates. It was not to b=
e and almost five months to the day since exiting a cup competition on pena=
lties following a curiously flat and uninspired display, Mikel Arteta=E2=80=
=99s side exited a cup competition on penalties following etc, and so on.</=
p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">Considering their team came into this game=
 on the back of consecutive defeats by Cheltenham and Exeter, Fleetwood=E2=
=80=99s Cod Army would almost certainly have settled for seeing their playe=
rs avoid embarrassment but after watching them go ahead against a team of F=
ancy Dans who were visibly labouring in the miserable conditions expectatio=
ns were duly raised. Arsenal equalised courtesy of a scrambled Viktor Gy=C3=
=B6keres effort that is unlikely to trouble the Puskas Award jury, before a=
ll hell broke loose when young Max Dowman was sent off for retaliation foll=
owing a Harrison Neal challenge that =E2=80=93 depending entirely on what t=
eam you support =E2=80=93 was a potential career-ender or wasn=E2=80=99t ev=
en a foul. While he is not yet old enough to drive, get a tattoo or vote, D=
owman has apparently been around long enough to earn himself a stinging reb=
uke from his manager, who <a href=3D"https://ablink.editorial.theguardian.c=
om/ss/c/u001.Yw_JkLMEmFuifc_XG18IRyTNtZQ7fIEMgszcCSneHEBgtjhYSJYcaNsDra0Bxn=
PgN_LWyUQCK6K11BofpytvXvZAAzDUQMONiEoalnyd8-9Wv5C-8abGpw_Aycq_HD0kkQN4A62an=
YM5aa9xCISJLQDtV5CVfWa7v88ZYRFo9VYj2Pgm2hPd2Scu6MVm2nutB9Krrqx1lk__PCwGUAlK=
wzxgAWrt2E6pzK6aq4WHUZyKEq6grKQXZoMS3hq3mILOP8yh34r4V786PC-YTd0kFmt_sV-s62o=
4Cn6QGBGoRYKZdhGXbeWSAJ30JnOB7L4r/4v9/3pYOUiw8S4qIg1fS742QQA/h28/h001.hgmh1=
rQkqlZScQzYnwhEW-L8EKVrY1gzJVuRtIRmo9A" style=3D"color: #0077B6;">conveyed =
the impression the 16-year-old could look forward to being sent to bed with=
out any supper</a> and having his screen-time vastly reduced.</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">A penalty shootout in which yet another Br=
azilian missed a crucial spot-kick for the Gunners ended in victory for Fle=
etwood, when Conor Haughey fired past Illan Meslier to make it five success=
ful kicks out of five for the hosts. The second teenager to disgrace himsel=
f on the night, the young man from Norn Iron proceeded to drop a different =
kind of F-bomb in a post-match interview with Sky Sports. Asked what had be=
en going through his mind before he took his penalty, Haughey replied: =E2=
=80=9CHit the top corner and run like f**k.=E2=80=9D</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">Despite the post-watershed lateness of the=
 hour, Sky=E2=80=99s pitchside reporter felt compelled to apologise to view=
ers for the youngster=E2=80=99s forthright response. While Arteta is left t=
o focus on making sure his players get their act together ahead of Sunday=
=E2=80=99s trip to Liverpool, Fleetwood head coach, Matt Lawlor, can look f=
orward to tonight=E2=80=99s quarter-final draw. =E2=80=9CI=E2=80=99ve got n=
o preference whatsoever,=E2=80=9D he said. =E2=80=9CWe=E2=80=99ve got a big=
 game at home [against Bristol Rovers] on Saturday and I want to win it. I =
would absolutely love to make an amazing night into an amazing week.=E2=80=
=9D For Arsenal, on a night when heroes were hard to find, the dream of a d=
omestic treble went its own way. =E2=80=8A</p>
